# CQ 18: Which model parameters does a model have?
#
# 3.3.8 defines the model parameter as an internal variable of a model that
# affects how it computes its outputs. Note 1 names the weights in a neural
# network as an example.
#
# Empty on test case 2, where the model carries hyperparameters instead. Read
# against question 12 the two show the difference: a model parameter is
# determined by training, a hyperparameter is chosen before it.
PREFIX iso:  <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#>
PREFIX inst: <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989/instances#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
SELECT ?model ?parameter
WHERE { ?model iso:hasParameter ?parameter }
ORDER BY ?model ?parameter
